---
alwaysApply: false
description: How to move files around
---

Moving a source code around is trivial, as it is enforced by the compiler,
which will finally be iterated into a healthy format.

Moving a document file `*.md` is tricky. You should carefully follow the
steps below:
1. Before moving the file, use `grep` this file name to find all the
   usages of this file. A path usage to this can either be:
   1. a relative path in markdown link, `[text](./relative/path/from/this/file)`,
   2. a absolute path in this project `assassyn/path/to/file`.
2. Match the file paths pointing to this file.
3. Rename them to the new path.
3. Move this file to the new destination.
